electron/laya — vendored Laya implementation
==========================================

Vendored from laya-mlx (Apache-2.0):
  Repository: https://github.com/mizchi/laya-mlx
  Source revision: dc3aa6b150cb861d0788fbd421cfd1303de4ed57
  Source directory: web/packages/laya-web/src

The following seven files are copied from that revision with import specifier
changes ("./x.ts" -> "./x", see README.md) and a provenance header added:

  types.ts
  pyjson.ts
  tokenizer.ts
  questions.ts
  prompt.ts
  calibration.ts
  agent.ts

Three of them carry local, behaviour-preserving changes on top of that, each
listed in its own provenance header:

  tokenizer.ts  `encode` memoizes its result in a bounded FIFO cache; the
                per-character `\p{White_Space}` regex became an equivalent
                code-point test; token accumulation uses index loops.
  prompt.ts     `buildSequence` accepts optional precomputed state ids.
  agent.ts      `prepare` encodes the shared state once and passes the ids to
                `buildSequence` instead of re-encoding per question.

Token ids, sequences and answers are unchanged; `tests/laya-tokenizer.test.ts`
pins that.

The tokenizer/sequence/answer parity test fixture
(tests/fixtures/laya-parity-multilingual.json) is also copied from that
revision, file web/fixtures/parity-multilingual.json.

